THE TEXTBOOK
The textbook is invented: its pages, wording, figure number and page numbers are made up for the film, and no publisher is
named. Facts on screen: the Earth is closest to the Sun (perihelion) in early January and farthest (aphelion) in early
July; the axis is tilted about 23.5° and keeps its direction through the year; seasons in the southern hemisphere are the
reverse of the north.
